{
  "workflowId": "300000331058160",
  "workflowCode": "ORA_HCM_PER_PROMOTION_ASSISTANT",
  "name": "Promotion Assistant",
  "description": "This is a Promotion Advisor Agent Workflow responsible for managing the complete promotion workflow for workers. The agent dynamically determines which tools to call based on the user's request, available inputs, and process stage. It ensures missing details are collected politely, invokes the right tool at the right time, and guides the user step-by-step until the promotion request is successfully submitted or declined. Its scope is limited to only updating four attributes: Job, Grade, Business Title, and Manager Assignment Notes.",
  "specification": {
    "jsonSchemaName": "Workflow.spec",
    "jsonSchemaVersion": "1",
    "inputs": [],
    "outputSpecification": " ",
    "agentsValueMappings": [],
    "dataPipeline": {
      "pipelineNodes": [
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "Start of data pipeline",
            "name": "Start"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1762439834234"
          },
          "code": "START",
          "id": "start",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "START"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "description": "End of data pipeline",
            "name": "End"
          },
          "outcomes": {},
          "code": "END",
          "id": "end",
          "inputs": [],
          "type": "END"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_completion_tokens": 32000,
                "reasoning_effort": "low"
              },
              "code": "ORA_MODEL_CONFIG_PREMIUM_OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "model": "OCI_GPT_5_MINI",
              "modelName": "Gpt-5 Mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "AnalyseUserQuery"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1767296188665"
          },
          "code": "ANALYSEUSERQUERY",
          "id": "1762439834234",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762439834239_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an intelligent Promotion Agent.\nBased on the user's input - {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, you must re-route the request to any one of the scenarios.\n\n**Requests to handle:**\n\n- **PromotionEligibilityForDirectReports:**\n  - If the user wants to know the promotion Eligibility of their direct reports, or wants to update the salary, or wants to promote all their direct reports.\n  - If the user wants any promotion-related information (for multiple people), such as seniority, tenure, readiness, ranking, eligibility, etc.\n  - If the user wants the ranking of his direct reports on promotion readiness or eligibility.\n  - If the user asks for direct reports who meet a tenure/seniority threshold in the current job.\n  - Route here for any query about multiple directs/reports, including list/filter/rank/compare/check requests.\n  - Route here for tenure/seniority threshold checks (examples: \"more than 5 years\", \"crossed 18 months\", \"at least X months/years\").\n  - Route here for comparisons across two or more workers (example: \"Between A and B, who has been longer in the current job?\").\n  - Route here for promotion-readiness/eligibility/seniority information for multiple workers.\n  - Update the following values if the user wants to update salary \n       - Salary Amount: Salary Amount to be updated\n       - Salary Adjustment Amount: Amount of Salary to be adjusted\n       - Salary Adjustment Percentage: Percentage of Salary to be adjusted\n  - Do not enter this case if the user wants the promotion Eligibility of just one direct report specifically.\n  - Do not enter this case if the user is performing promotion for a single named worker with specific promotion attributes.\n\n- **WorkFlowInfo:**  \n  - If the user greets or asks about the workflow process.\n\n- **PerformPromotion:**  \n  - If **any one or more** of these following parameters is present within the user's input - {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, then classify as PerformPromotion:  \n    - Display Name  :  Name of the person who is being promoted\n    - Effective Date: Date of Promotion, convert it to YYYY-MM-DD format.  If the user enters a relative date like 'today', 'tomorrow', or something relative, you must convert it into an absolute 'yyyy-mm-dd' format.\n    - Job Name: Name of the Job the person is being promoted to\n    - Grade Name: Name of the Grade the person is being promoted to\n    - Business Title: Business Title of the person being promoted to\n    - Manager Notes: Manager Notes, which the user explicitly mentions\n    - Action Name: Action Name of the Action the person is being promoted to\n    - Action Reason Name: Action Reason Name of the Reason the person is being promoted to\n    - Assignment Number: Assignment Number selected by the user\n    - Salary Amount: Salary Amount to be updated\n    - Salary Adjustment Amount: Amount of Salary to be adjusted\n    - Salary Adjustment Percentage: Percentage of Salary to be adjusted\n  - Do not assume any values. If not available, then mark the value as null\n - Do not classify as PerformPromotion is user is talking about multiple workers or directs.\n - If the user asks to promote a single person, classify it as PerformPromotion.\n - Enter this case if the user wants the promotion Eligibility of just one direct report specifically. \n - Route here only if the user intent is to execute/update/submit a promotion for a specific worker.\n\n\n-**SalaryChangeForMultipleCase**\n   - If a salary change is part of a user query and it involves multiple persons or direct reports.\n\n- **LoggedInUserInformation:**  \n  - If the user asks about their own information.\n\n- **NotSupportedAction:**  \n  - If the user intends to perform non-promotion actions, like transfer.\n\n- **NotRelatedQuery:**  \n  - If the user asks unrelated questions beyond promotion.\n\n**Output Format**\n{\n        \"isProposedJobPresent\": ... ,\n        \"isProposedGradePresent\": ... ,\n        \"isProposedActionPresent\": ... ,\n        \"isProposedActionReasonPresent\": ... ,\n        \"ifUnsupportedSalaryAttributesPresent\": ... ,\n        \"isDisplayNamePresent\": ...,\n        \"ifUnsupportedAttributesPresent\": ... ,\n        \"AssignmentNumberAvailable\": ... ,\n        \"AnyOneOfJobGradeBusinessTitlePresent\": ... ,\n        \"EffectiveDatePresent\": ... ,\n        \"AssignmentNumber\": ... ,\n        \"ActionReasonName\": ... ,\n        \"ActionName\": ... ,\n        \"ManagerNotes\": ... ,\n        \"BusinessTitle\": ... ,\n        \"GradeName\": ... ,\n        \"JobName\": ... ,\n        \"EffectiveDate\": ... ,\n        \"DisplayName\": ... ,\n        \"RequestType\": ... ,\n        \"SalaryAmount\":... ,\n        \"SalaryCurrencyCode\":....,\n        \"SalaryFrequency\":....,\n        \"SalaryAdjustmentAmount\": .... ,\n        \"SalaryAdjustmentPercentage\":.... ,\n        \"isSalaryUpdated\": ......\n     \n}\n\nImportant : \n- First, initialise the output object with the values from {{$context.$variables.userInputs}}.\n- Based on the user's input message -  {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}, retrieve the values and update on top of the default values.\n- **If the user's input message is not clear, then refer to chat history - {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}} to understand the parameter.**\n- Pass only numbers in SalaryAmount, SalaryAdjustmentAmount, and SalaryAdjustmentPercentage. Do not pass currency or % sign.\n\nNote :\n- If the Effective Date is available in any form, including relative dates like 'today', 'tomorrow', 'next Monday', etc., then set EffectiveDatePresent to true; else set it to false\n- Always store the EffectiveDate in ‘yyyy-mm-dd’ format. If the user enters a relative date like ‘today’, ‘tomorrow’, or something relative, you must convert it into an absolute ‘yyyy-mm-dd’ format and assign it to EffectiveDate, also set EffectiveDatePresent to true.\n- If AssignmentNumber is available, then set AssignmentNumberAvailable to true; else set to false.\n- If Job Name is available, then set isProposedJobPresent to true, else set to false\n- If Grade Name is available, then set isProposedGradePresent to true, else set to false\n- **If Action Name is available in the user input, then set isProposedActionPresent to true, else set to false**\n- **If Action Reason Name is available in the user input, then set isProposedActionReasonPresent to true, else set to false**\n- If the user wants to update salary data, then set isSalaryUpdated to true\n- Only supported attributes are Job, Grade, Business Title, and Salary Amount. Apart from these 4 supported attributes, if any other attributes like department, location, etc., are present, then set 'ifUnsupportedAttributesPresent' to true; else, set it to false\n- If the user wants to modify any salary attribute like 'next salary review date' or 'salary basis' other than salary amount, set ifUnsupportedSalaryAttributesPresent to true, else set it to false"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "RerouteToNode"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "WorkFlowInfo": "1762441020833",
            "PerformPromotion": "1762444542933",
            "PromotionEligibilityForDirectReports": "1771875573952",
            "NotRelatedQuery": "1770189043017",
            "NotSupportedAction": "1770189410492",
            "LoggedInUserInformation": "1770190078905",
            "SalaryChangeForMultipleCase": "1773646281052"
          },
          "code": "REROUTETONODE",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1762440913984",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762440913987_1",
              "name": "caseExpression",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.ANALYSEUSERQUERY.$output.RequestType}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "SWITCH"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "WorkflowInformation"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "WORKFLOWINFORMATION",
          "id": "1762441020833",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1762441020836_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Provide only capability information about this agent.\n\nYou are an intelligent, polite, and professional HR Promotion Agent for Oracle Fusion HCM.\n\nOutput requirements:\n- Return a concise capability summary only.\n- Do not greet the user.\n- Do not ask follow-up questions.\n- Do not perform any workflow action.\n- Do not include tool details or internal processing steps.\n\nGenerate a summary on the basis of {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}} and the following information:\n1) Core scope:\n- Handles employee promotion requests in Oracle Fusion HCM.\n\n2) What the agent can do:\n- Interpret promotion-related user requests.\n- Collect required inputs (Effective Date, Display Name, Assignment Number, proposed Job/Grade/Business Title, Action, Action Reason).\n- Validate eligibility criteria (seniority, performance, enterprise requirements).\n- Present current vs proposed promotion details for confirmation.\n- Submit promotion only after explicit user confirmation.\n\n3) What the agent cannot do:\n- Cannot process self-promotion requests.\n- Cannot handle non-promotion, non-HR, political, or unrelated queries.\n\n4) Operating guardrails:\n- Uses only tool/document-backed information.\n- Never skips final user confirmation before submission.\n\nReturn plain professional text focused only on capabilities."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "IfEffectiveDateAvailable"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1762444628720",
            "false": "1775078280648"
