            {
              "id": "1762448071134_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Display these Worker Assignment records to the user in an HTML Table.\nDisplay all attributes in the table, but set the HTML hidden attribute on \"AssignmentId\" and \"PersonId\" because they are sensitive fields that are still required in the chat history. So, include them in the HTML table as hidden inputs.\nDo not show the Assignment ID or Person ID for the user\nAlways display only the HTML table; no HTML tags should be shown to the user at any time.\n\nGenerate the table in HTML with:\n1. A row number column as the first column\n2. border: 2px solid black applied to table, th, and td\n3. border-collapse: collapse\n4. Header row text in bold\n5. Alternating row background colors:\n#FFFFFF (white)\n#F2F2F2 (light grey)\n6. Row numbering must remain correct even if rows are filtered or sorted.\n7. The Column headers must also be #F2F2F2 (light grey) color.\n8. Only the following columns need to be visible in the table and in the following table: \"Number, Display Name, Business Title, Person Number, Assignment Number\".\n\nBelow the table, after adding one line break (i.e., after adding a <br> tag), add this text exactly: \"Please choose one record by providing the Assignment Number\". This is not part of the table at all\n\nWorker Assignment Records to be Displayed in an HTML table:\n {{$context.$variables.WorkerSearchResponse.partialMatchingRecords}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        }
